/**
 * @cutiepage/template-sdk — public surface.
 * docs/BLUEPRINT_TEMPLATE_PACKAGES.md §4.
 *
 * THE SURFACE IS FROZEN PER MAJOR (§4, §14.8). A package declares
 * `runtime.sdk: "^1.0.0"`; the platform may ship 1.x ADDITIVELY, and 2.0 means
 * old packages keep running against the 1.x runtime, which stays served.
 * Breaking this breaks every uploaded template at once — a larger blast radius
 * than any single app change. Add; never remove or repurpose.
 *
 * The runtime provides these as externals, so the SDK is never bundled into a
 * package (§4) — which is also why an author's `import` of it is on the
 * validator's allowed-externals list.
 */

